// jctkac: a function whose declared return type is an enum spells its C type from
// the return-annotation tid (c_type_from_tid), not the flat get_fn_enum_ret head
// (c_type_from_tag) or the ann_mono_stem carrier. Two emit sites route enum returns
// through the enum branch: emit_fn_decl (sig_ret_decl_enum) and emit_fn_def
// (sig_ret_def_enum). Each formerly spelled the return with
// c_type_from_tag(enum_ret) for a plain enum and c_type_c_name(ret_stem) for a
// generic-enum instance; the tid channel spells the same name at both, so the read
// now moves to the tid directly (the flat spelling stays only as the probe arg).
//
// The functions below are the plain-enum coverage: a bare enum return (Col), a
// conditionally-returned enum (Dir), and an enum returned through a nested call
// (relay). Each body reads the returned variant back, so a wrong or empty return
// spelling would fail to compile or compare the wrong tag. The generic-enum
// INSTANCE sub-path of this branch (`-> Tree[Int]`) is not runtime-pinned here: it
// hits a separate, pre-existing typedef emit-order defect that makes such returns
// fail at cc, so its tid==flat equivalence is proven at the emit level (the
// generated C is unchanged by the conversion) rather than by running it. The
// plain-enum flat and tid spellings resolve to the same string, so these rows are
// a characterization pin plus a regression guard against a future tid-decline at an
// enum-return position (which would emit an empty return type rather than the flat
// head).

type Col { Red, Green, Blue }
type Dir { North, South, East, West }

fn plain_enum() -> Col { Col.Green }

fn pick_dir(n: Int) -> Dir {
    if n == 0 { North } else { if n == 1 { South } else { East } }
}

fn relay(n: Int) -> Dir { pick_dir(n) }

test "plain enum return carries the variant" {
    assert(plain_enum() == Col.Green)
    match plain_enum() {
        Green => assert(true)
        Red => assert(false)
        Blue => assert(false)
    }
}

test "conditionally-returned enum carries the chosen variant" {
    assert(pick_dir(0) == Dir.North)
    assert(pick_dir(1) == Dir.South)
    assert(pick_dir(9) == Dir.East)
}

test "enum returned through a nested call round-trips" {
    assert(relay(0) == Dir.North)
    assert(relay(1) == Dir.South)
    assert(relay(2) == Dir.East)
}
